This Privacy Policy explains how information is collected, used, and safeguarded when you play the mobile application Dreams Puzzle Adventure ("the Game").

By downloading and using the Game, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy.

1. Information Collection and Use
Dreams Puzzle Adventure does not directly collect, store, or require personal identification information (such as your name, physical address, email address, or phone number).

However, to provide advertisements, analyze gameplay performance, and improve the user experience, certain non-personal technical data may be automatically processed through third-party services:

Device Data: Device model, operating system version, and unique device identifiers (e.g., Advertising ID / IDFA).

Usage & Diagnostic Data: In-game progress, session durations, crash logs, and general performance metrics.

2. Third-Party Services
The Game integrates third-party Software Development Kits (SDKs) to facilitate advertising, analytics, and platform services. These third parties collect and process data governed by their respective privacy policies:

Google Play Services (Achievements and Leaderboards)

Unity Ads / Google AdMob (In-game advertising display)

Unity Analytics / Firebase (App performance and crash reporting)

These third-party networks may use your device's Advertising ID to deliver relevant ads and maintain service reliability.

3. Children's Privacy
We are committed to protecting the privacy of young players. The Game does not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from children under the age of 13 (or the applicable age limit in your jurisdiction). If you become aware that a child has provided personal information without parental consent, please contact us so we can promptly delete such data.

4. Data Security
We value your trust and strive to handle data responsibly. While we do not harvest personal details directly, all automated technical telemetry relies on industry-standard security measures implemented by our third-party SDK partners.

5. Changes to This Privacy Policy
This Privacy Policy may be updated periodically. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated "Last Updated" date. You are advised to review this Privacy Policy periodically for any changes.
